'''Calligraphy Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] added in [[Version 11.0 Update|Version 11.0]] who can be unlocked when beating the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[Aku Reincarnation (Merciless)|Rashomon]] appearing on the '''11th''', '''12th''', '''25th''' and '''26th''' of every month.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 630
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Calligraphy Cat
|name2 = Tea Master Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Tea Master Cat''' at Level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Calligraphy Cat can be considered a '''much''' more situational version of pre-[[Talents]] [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. In comparison to them, Tea Master Cat has lower range, lower stats, and a slower recharge on top of [[Single Attack]], but has immunities to [[Wave Attack]]s and [[Surge Attack]]s, a lower cost, and {{4c}} usability in exchange. His Surge and Wave immunities usually aren't that useful since enemies with these abilities typically feature extreme damage or outrange him, but they work well against the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]] and [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]], and can allow him to avoid the waves from [[Haniwanwan]] (though Haniwanwan is usually dealt with using Wave Blockers).

He can also see some actual use in [[Infernal Tower]]'s [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|30th floor]], since he's Strong against [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]], and immune to both his Waves and the [[Sinner Snache]]s' [[Surge Attack#Death Surge|Death Surges]]. That's about the limit of his usefulness, though, because in most other situations, he's outclassed by Slapsticks. For example, in the [[Infernal Tower/Floor 50|50th floor]] of Infernal Tower, Slapsticks is typically used over Calligraphy in spite of his Surge Immunity because of their superior range, damage output and Area Attack.

Tragically, Calligraphy Cat can't even catch a break in {{4c}}, where Slapsticks can't be used. There, better options such as [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] or [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] do miles better than him in terms of usefulness against Relics. That's not even mentioning the [[True Form]]s of [[Uncanny Legends]] drop units, such as [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ape Lord Luza]] or [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]], who are infinitely more useful anti-Relic units than Calligraphy Cat. In the end, Calligraphy Cat is a near-useless unit held back by horrendous stats even when factoring in Strong.

